### EC Eligibility

| Check | Status |
|---|---|
| First-timer family nucleus (married couple) | ✅ |
| Family nucleus with dependants (2 kids) | ✅ strengthens |
| Income ≤ $16,000 ceiling | ✅ — at the exact limit |
| Must not own / have disposed of private property in past 30 months | Verify |
| Must not have received HDB housing subsidy before | Verify |

**Income at the ceiling is a risk.** HDB uses the average gross income over the preceding 12 months. If either partner has variable pay (commissions, bonuses), the average must still sit ≤ $16,000. One month over doesn't disqualify but the average must comply.

---

### CPF Housing Grant (EC)

The CPF Housing Grant for EC is income-tiered and phases out well before the $16,000 income ceiling:

| Combined income | Family Grant (SC-SC) |
|---|---|
| ≤ $10,000 | $30,000 |
| $10,001 – $11,000 | $25,000 |
| $11,001 – $12,000 | $20,000 |
| $12,001 – $13,000 | $15,000 |
| $13,001 – $14,000 | $10,000 |
| $14,001 – $15,000 | $5,000 |
| **> $15,000** | **$0** |

At $16,000 combined income: **no CPF Housing Grant expected.** Verify against current HDB tables — tiers are adjusted periodically.

SC-PR couple: same tiers apply but the cap drops to $20,000 maximum even at lower income bands.

EHG (Enhanced Housing Grant) does **not** apply to EC — that is HDB-flat-only.

---

